INT. COMPANY BREAK ROOM, INNOVATEX CORP - DAY

Beige walls. A coffee machine with a handwritten sign: DO NOT USE. A bulletin board layered with expired memos. The microwave hums. A mini fridge stickered with passive-aggressive notes.

GLORIA BANKOLE-VANCE (50s, shoulder pads, mug reading WORLD'S OKAYEST BOSS) refills her mug from a thermos she brought herself. Across the table sits COLIN DRUMMOND-PARK (20s, new hire, ironed shirt). At the sink, SHANTELLE OKONJO-REID (30s, hoodie, headphones) scrubs a mug that isn't hers.

GLORIA
Colin, welcome to the family.

COLIN
Thank you, Gloria.

GLORIA
We do synergy here.

COLIN
Great.

GLORIA
We also do Fridays.

COLIN
Fridays?

SHANTELLE
(over her shoulder)
She means cake.

GLORIA
I mean team-building.

SHANTELLE
It's cake.

Gloria beams. Colin tries to look as though he understands.
